# core_numeric -- interpretive arithmetic of INTERPRETER.agc (Comanche055
# pp.1131-1191) run through the real INTPRET entry, for tests/oracle_core_numeric.c.
#
# Each run pokes a 3-word snippet into VAC2USE (first opcode word [+ operand
# words], EXIT 77776, TC ENDOFJOB) and its operands into the VAC1 work area
# (FIXLOC = PUSHLOC = VAC1): first operand at 10D (DP/TP/vector), second at
# 12D (DP), 14D (TP) or 16D (vector), scalar for VXSC/V/SC and matrix for
# MXV/VXM at 22D. Opcode words from yaYUL; shift counts are operand words
# (SR n = 20600+n+1, SRR = 21600+n+1, SL = 20200+n+1, octal).
# The run tag is "OP,input,input,..." with inputs as signed integers
# (DP: value * 2^28, TP: value * 2^42, vectors x,y,z, matrix row-major,
# shift count last).  Outputs: MPAC (TP), MPAC+3/+5 (vector y, z), OVFIND,
# VAC1+30 (NORM count), LVSQUARE (34D) and LV (36D), FAILREG (ALARM 01301).
#
# Cases where stock yaAGC hits its DV emulation bug (a -0 minor word in L is
# taken as a borrow by SpToDecent, so the quotient is one major LSB low)
# were dropped; see docs/modules/core-numeric.md "Open questions".
